<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nova Scotia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nova Scotia is a province on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, originally part of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> acquired it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> in 1713, along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asiento">asiento</a>. These gains marked an important stage in the growth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nova-scotia.jpg" alt="Nova Scotia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Kooma, FJDEACKB, Zscout370 and Denelson83 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nova_Scotia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
